    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0461" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg401"/>

                <head>Mr. Plumb to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 16, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reply to your dispatch No. 25,
                    of the 26th of November last, relating to Captain Krauseneck, I have now to add,
                    in addition to what was stated in my No. 52, of the 18th ultimo, that I am
                    informed <pb facs="0462" n="402" xml:id="pg402"/> that officer left this country
                    for Europe by the French steamer from Vera Cruz on the 13th of last month.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. L. PLUMB.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
